  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-rc.2\n\n\t\tFramework alignment release. No changes to this package's own surface: components, models and the browser assets are unchanged from 1.0.0-rc.1.\n\n\t\t=== Why the version moved ==================================================\n\t\t- The family moves onto the Agent Framework 1.18.0 line so the core package can adopt AgentSkillsSource (skills from any source) and the ToolApprovalAgent middleware (auto-approval). All five packages ship together and share one version.\n\t\t- Microsoft.Extensions.AI moves to 10.7.0 here to match.\n\n\t\t=== Unchanged, and worth restating ========================================\n\t\t- The XSS boundary, the 10-language string table, the CSS variable contract and the widget's script and stylesheet are exactly as in rc.1, and the 182 component tests plus 106 JavaScript assertions that pin them still pass unchanged against the new framework line.",
